--When **Claude Code** is selected in the Prioritize-from-README agent picker, the request now authenticates with the claude.ai subscription OAuth token instead of a stored Claude API key.
-+Resolves the ad-hoc request on the Agents tab.
- 
--Previously the code read the Claude API key first and only fell back to the OAuth token when that key was empty, so a user signed in to Claude Code who also had an API key configured hit the metered API and failed with `HTTP 400: Your credit balance is too low`.
-+## Advance to the next agent on delete
-+Deleting an agent from the list now advances the selection to the next row
-+(or the previous one when the last row is removed) instead of snapping back
-+to the top of the list. Works for both stored sessions and external
-+(watch-only) rows.
- 
--- `claude-code` now uses the OAuth token exclusively (ignores any stored API key)
--- Clearer "Sign in to Claude Code first" notice when no token is found
--- `Claude API` and `OpenAI API` keep using their own keys
-+## Model picker in "Start a new agent"
-+A second dropdown sits beside the agent (Claude Code) picker, listing the
-+available LLM models. The chosen model is actually used:
-+- Claude Code path: passed to the `claude` CLI as `--model`.
-+- API-key providers (Claude API / OpenAI API): set as the runner's model
-+  override.
-+
-+The model list follows the selected provider, and "Default model" leaves the
-+provider's own default untouched.
-+
-+## Verify
-+- Open a repo's Agents tab, select an agent, Delete -> selection moves to the
-+  next agent rather than the first.
-+- In "Start a new agent", pick a model and start a Claude Code run; the agent
-+  launches with `--model <chosen>`.
-+
-+Build and the forkmesh-tests + forkmesh-window-tests suites pass.
